  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/... \nWith strong dry air advection in place behind the departing trough, \nweather conditions will turn much quieter beginning Friday. A piece \nof energy left behind from departing trough is currently being \ndepicted by the model guidance to separate itself from the main jet \nenergy and briefly morph into a cut-off low over AZ during the \nweekend. This feature for the most part should be inconsequential, \nalthough enough moisture could be present for some showers to \nmaterialize over the AZ high terrain on Saturday but for the most \npart should remain on the light side given the overall lack of \ninstability that will be present. The lower deserts should remain \nrain-free as there will be too much dry air in place. Under the \npresence of the low, temperatures will be several degrees below \nnormal during the weekend with afternoon highs struggling to reach \n80 degrees across the lower deserts. As the upper-level low exits \nthe region and weak ridging builds overhead early next week, \ntemperatures will rebound to more seasonal levels.",
